Recall the difference formula for tangent:

$$
\tan\left(x - y\right) = \frac{\tan x - \tan y}{1 + \tan x\tan y}
$$

Apply it with $x=150^\circ$ and $y=135^\circ$. The special-angle values are $\tan\left(150^\circ\right)=-\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}$ and $\tan\left(135^\circ\right)=-1$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan\left(15^\circ\right) &= \tan\left(150^\circ - 135^\circ\right) \\
&= \frac{\tan\left(150^\circ\right) - \tan\left(135^\circ\right)}{1 + \tan\left(150^\circ\right)\tan\left(135^\circ\right)} \\
&= \frac{\left(-\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\right) - \left(-1\right)}{1 + \left(-\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\right)\left(-1\right)}
\end{aligned}
$$

Multiply the numerator and denominator by $3$ to clear the fractions:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan\left(15^\circ\right) &= \frac{3\left(\left(-\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\right) - \left(-1\right)\right)}{3\left(1 + \left(-\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\right)\left(-1\right)\right)} \\
&= \frac{3 - \sqrt{3}}{3 + \sqrt{3}}
\end{aligned}
$$

Multiply by the conjugate of the denominator, expand, and simplify:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan\left(15^\circ\right) &= \frac{3 - \sqrt{3}}{3 + \sqrt{3}}\cdot \frac{3 - \sqrt{3}}{3 - \sqrt{3}} \\
&= \frac{\left(3 - \sqrt{3}\right)\left(3 - \sqrt{3}\right)}{\left(3 + \sqrt{3}\right)\left(3 - \sqrt{3}\right)} \\
&= \frac{12 - 6\sqrt{3}}{6} \\
&= 2 - \sqrt{3}
\end{aligned}
$$

Recall the difference formula for tangent:

$$
